{
  "raw": {
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4898": {
      "title": "Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Finance",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Finance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Finance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To receive full consideration, interested individuals must apply electronically. Applications should include a letter of application, resume or curriculum vita, and evidence to fulfill the following expectations: ○ Excellence in teaching finance courses. ○ Significant experience in the finance industry. Complete information regarding the required application process is available on-line at https://employment.bryant.edu/ Bryant University will begin reviewing applications immediately and will be conducting interviews starting in March. Should you wish to discuss this opening or request more information please contact Dr. Kevin Maloney, kmaloney2@bryant.edu , Chair of the Department of Finance. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Finance Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Faculty Reports To Dean, College of Business Position Summary Bryant University seeks to fill a Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty position in Finance. The successful candidate will have a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and to being an active member of the Finance Department faculty during their time at Bryant University. While we will consider applications from candidates with expertise in all areas of finance, we have a particular need for an individual who could teach at least two of the following undergraduate courses: Financial Management, Financial Institutions and Markets, Real Estate Finance, Risk Management and Insurance, Financial Planning, or Debt Securities. Descriptions of these courses can be accessed via the Course Catalogue on the Bryant website. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030 , redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities Research Data Support Bryant subscribes to the typical databases used in financial research (e.g., CRSP , Compustat), plus a number of specialized data services in support of research on corporate governance, banking, investments, and ESG topics. We utilize the WRDS platform at Bryant to organize our research databases. Bryant also provides access to FactSet, Morningstar, and Bloomberg to support research and teaching in Finance in our state of the art Financial Markets Center. Appointment The title will be Lecturer or Assistant Teaching Professor in Finance and salary will be based on the candidate qualifications, consistent with AACSB benchmarks. Ideally, the appointment would commence starting in the Fall 2027 semester, but an appointment starting in Spring 2027 semester may also be considered. Bryant University provides an inclusive and welcoming educational and working environment for all members of its community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual preference or orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, ethnicity, disability, genetic information, protected veteran, or marital status. Qualifications Candidates must have at least a Master’s Degree in Finance or a related field from an AACSB -International or EQUIS accredited institution. Prior teaching experience in a business school is also required. Relevant industry or regulatory experience in finance is desirable. Candidates should be open to participating in service activities, such as admission events, campus conferences, and student mentoring at Bryant University. Working Environment Bryant University is a 163-year-old private institution that is accredited by AACSB -International and the New England Commission of Higher Education ( NECHE ). Bryant is a student-centered institution, dedicated to educating and inspiring students to discover their passion, become innovative leaders with character, and make a difference around the world. Our innovative academic programs are attuned to the needs of industry and society with a strong commitment to experiential learning We have approximately 3,600 undergraduate students from 38 states and 40 countries. We also have approximately 400 full- and part-time graduate students. The Finance Department currently consists of ten tenured or tenure-track faculty members, six full-time non-tenure track members, and several adjunct professors. Due to high student demand for our courses and programs, we are seeking to grow the size of the full-time Finance Department faculty. Students interested in Finance can earn concentrations in finance as part of our undergraduate degrees in business administration ( BSBA ) or international business ( BSIB ). We also offer a specialized concentration in financial services for undergraduate students, and we offer graduate courses in Finance as part of Master’s degree programs. Bryant does not have a doctoral program in Finance. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC01646 Open Date 10/19/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions To receive full consideration, interested individuals must apply electronically. Applications should include a letter of application, resume or curriculum vita, and evidence to fulfill the following expectations: ○ Excellence in teaching finance courses. ○ Significant experience in the finance industry. Complete information regarding the required application process is available on-line at https://employment.bryant.edu/ Bryant University will begin reviewing applications immediately and will be conducting interviews starting in March. Should you wish to discuss this opening or request more information please contact Dr. Kevin Maloney, kmaloney2@bryant.edu , Chair of the Department of Finance. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Teaching Evaluation(s) Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4897": {
      "title": "Professional in Residence, Global Supply Chain Management",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Professional in Residence, Global Supply Chain Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Professional in Residence, Global Supply Chain Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Professional in Residence, Global Supply Chain Management Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Faculty Reports To Chair, Department of Management Position Summary Bryant University’s College of Business invites applications for a Professional in Residence of Global Supply Chain Management ( GSCM ). This individual should demonstrate excellence in teaching courses in supply chain management, including the integration of AI. It is expected that this position will serve as Program Coordinator of the Global Supply Chain Management Program. This is a full-time, non-tenure track, renewable position. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030 , redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities The successful candidate will be expected to teach in our undergraduate ( BSBA ) as well as graduate ( MBA ) programs related to Global Supply Chain Management and possibly Operations Management. The area of specialization/certification that will be given preference for this position is Supply Chain Management ( SCM ). Applicants will be expected to have expertise in a SCM -related function (e.g. logistics, operations management, planning, sourcing, forecasting, and strategy) and demonstrate a proven ability to engage in an environment that emphasizes cross-functional interaction and integration, both within and outside traditional supply chain management areas. Areas where expertise is desired include (but are not limited to) healthcare operations and management, supply chain strategy, analytics, operations management, and global sourcing. Candidates with expertise in international trade and logistics are highly desired. The successful candidate will teach the high profile GSCM Practicum course, which involves semester-long consulting projects with industry clients. It is expected that the candidate will have industry experience and an existing network of potential contacts from whom some of the capstone projects might be solicited. In addition, the candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses involving International Trade and Logistics. The position is ideal for an industry professional seeking strong teaching experience in an applied, student-centered environment. The successful candidate will also demonstrate the potential to lead the GSCM program, establishing connections with the business community, participating in the development of new courses, building new programs, and enhancing the student experience. The position involves active participant in departmental and institutional activities. Qualifications Candidates must have an MBA or Master’s Degree in a relevant area from an AACSB -International accredited school. Candidates should be committed to teaching excellence and serving as an active member of the Bryant community. The successful candidate must be able to teach courses at both the undergraduate ( BSBA ) and graduate ( MBA ) level. In addition: Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching undergraduate and graduate supply chain management, including international trade and logistics or related quantitative/analytical courses. Substantial industry experience and a willingness to cultivate and engage industry for teaching experience and student practicum consulting project opportunities. Prior teaching experience, especially in Supply Chain Management, International Trade and Logistics, Operations Management or analytics courses. Ability to integrate AI in Supply Chain Management courses Work with the Dean, Department Chair and GSCM colleagues as the Global Supply Chain Management Program Coordinator, which includes: arrange and facilitate regular events for GSCM students involving, but not limited to, Networking Night, guest speakers, and lunches with executives. Engage and help guide the student supply chain club, SCLA (Supply Chain Leadership Association). Strong communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work effectively with diverse student populations and contribute to an inclusive learning environment. Ability to work comfortably with technology and analytics. Demonstrated ability to use active learning and incorporate experiential activities. Potential for ongoing, long-term contribution to Bryant University’s teaching mission. Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC01645 Open Date 10/16/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Teaching Evaluation(s) Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4896": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Biomedical Sciences and Human Biology",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor in Biomedical Sciences and Human Biology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Assistant Professor in Biomedical Sciences and Human Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor in Biomedical Sciences and Human Biology Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Faculty Reports To Dean, College of Health and Behavioral Sciences Position Summary Bryant University’s College of Health and Behavioral Sciences seeks a tenure-track faculty member with expertise in human biology, physiology, or the cellular and molecular mechanisms of human health and disease, and a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and student mentorship. Position Overview The successful candidate will contribute to our growing programs in biology and health sciences, with primary teaching responsibilities in Human Anatomy and Physiology I and II, including lecture and laboratory instruction. Additional teaching opportunities include introductory biology, cellular and molecular biology, organismal biology, human health and disease, and research methods in health sciences, depending on expertise and departmental needs. We seek an educator-scholar who connects foundational science to human health and professional practice, and engages students through applied learning and undergraduate research. The ideal candidate will develop a research program that complements our existing strengths in bacteriology, chemical biology, exercise physiology, AI, and biomedical sciences and draws on our shared analytical core facility, which includes mass spectrometry, chromatography, and new NIH -funded tissue culture and microscopy facilities. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030 , redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities Research Expectations Bryant University values faculty scholarship that involves undergraduate students. The successful candidate’s research should: Focus on cellular, molecular, or physiological mechanisms of human health and disease. Research integrating AI to advance understanding of human health and disease is preferred. Develop a biomedical research program that advances understanding of human health and disease and aligns with RI-INBRE’s mission to strengthen biomedical research capacity and student research training. Utilize shared analytical equipment and foster collaboration with existing faculty. Engage undergraduate researchers in meaningful, accessible research experiences, and serve as a mentor for students interested in health-related careers, both clinical and non-clinical. RI- INBRE PUI Faculty Scholar The successful candidate may be considered for designation as an RI- INBRE PUI Faculty Scholar, a program designed to recruit and support early-career investigators who bring new biomedical research expertise to primarily undergraduate institutions and Rhode Island. Designation is subject to RI- INBRE review and approval of the candidate’s research program. RI- INBRE PUI Faculty Scholars are eligible to apply for supplemental research funding to support laboratory establishment and the development of their research program and have full access to the RI- INBRE Centralized Research Core Facility. For more information about RI- INBRE see https://web.uri.edu/riinbre/. Qualifications Ph.D. in physiology, anatomy, biology, biomedical sciences, microbiology, cell biology, molecular biology, neuroscience, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated preparation to teach the full Human Anatomy and Physiology I and II sequence, including human anatomy, organ systems physiology, and associated laboratories. Research background in cellular, molecular, or physiological mechanisms of human health and disease. Demonstrated success with integration of AI into teaching and/or research. Commitment to undergraduate teaching, student mentorship, and the development of experiential learning opportunities. Evidence of potential for scholarly productivity involving undergraduate students. Application Materials: Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching statement, research statement, teaching evaluations (if available), and contact information for two references. The teaching statement should describe the applicant’s preparation to teach Human Anatomy and Physiology I and II, including laboratory instruction, and how they integrate or plan to integrate AI and experiential learning into their teaching to strengthen students’ understanding and application of scientific concepts. The research statement should describe a proposed research program and opportunities for meaningful undergraduate participation. Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC01644 Open Date 10/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Research Statement Optional Documents Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Teaching Evaluation(s) Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4888": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty, Doctoral Program in Clinical Psychology (Psy.D.)",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Clinical Faculty, Doctoral Program in Clinical Psychology (Psy.D.) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Clinical Faculty, Doctoral Program in Clinical Psychology (Psy.D.) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. If interested, please apply online and submit the following materials: cover letter, CV, teaching statement. With questions, contact the search chair, Christina Tortolani, PhD - ctortolani@bryant.edu Posting Details Position Information Job Title Clinical Faculty, Doctoral Program in Clinical Psychology (Psy.D.) Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Faculty Reports To Dean, College of Health and Behavioral Sciences Position Summary Bryant University’s Department of Psychology invites applications for a full-time, Clinical Faculty position in its Doctoral Program in Clinical Psychology (Psy.D.) . The Department of Psychology has undergone considerable growth in recent years and is excited to offer a high-level graduate program to train health service psychologists to better address the national behavioral health crisis. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to the program’s development with a team of dedicated and passionate faculty and academic leaders. The exceptional candidate will have a strong commitment to and passion for fostering the growth and development of graduate students, both academically and professionally. Opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration are encouraged with the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies, the Master of Science in Healthcare Informatics and AI, along with additional programs in the College of Health and Behavioral Sciences as well as the College of Humanities and Social Sciences and the College of Business. Rhode Island and Southeastern New England have robust healthcare systems that offer opportunities to forge quality partnerships and develop excellent training and research opportunities. The Psychology department is a flagship department in the growing College of Health and Behavioral Sciences at Bryant University, which currently offers undergraduate majors in Psychology, Biology, Health Sciences, and Exercise and Movement Science, as well as graduate programs in Physician Assistant Studies and Healthcare Informatics and AI. Our dedicated faculty and newly renovated and expanded psychology space prepare students for science-related careers and graduate studies. We emphasize basic and applied research, technological applications (especially related to applications of artificial intelligence), and real-world experiences so students not only accumulate knowledge but also develop the commitment and desire to apply what they learn in the field. Find out more about us at: https://www.bryant.edu/undergraduate/academics/college-health-and-behavioral-sciences Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030 , redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities The Department of Psychology in the College of Health and Behavioral Sciences is seeking a full-time Clinical Faculty member for its Doctoral Program in Clinical Psychology (Psy.D.). This individual will teach, advise, and provide research supervision within the Psy.D. program. Applications will be evaluated beginning October 30th. Responsibilities and Duties: Teach graduate courses in the PsyD program Participate in academic advising and mentorship of doctoral research projects Assist in the ongoing development of the Psy.D. program, including curriculum updates, strategic planning, and admissions and accreditation processes, among others. Scholarly activity that contributes to the field of clinical psychology is encouraged and preferred. Ongoing professional development, training, and involvement in professional organizations Qualifications Required Qualifications: Earned doctorate in clinical or counseling psychology from an APA -accredited program Completion of an APA -accredited internship Experience in clinical practice, teaching clinical psychology, and scholarly activity Licensed or eligible for licensure as a psychologist in Rhode Island Demonstrated use of innovative and effective teaching practices Excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills Demonstrated capacity for collaboration, team building, self-direction, and innovation in educational programming Commitment to preparing students to serve individuals from all cultural backgrounds and to strengthening the behavioral health workforce Preferred Qualifications: Ongoing involvement in clinical practice, which is encouraged and supported by the University Deep knowledge of evidence-based practices Experience in one or more of the following areas: health psychology, child and adolescent psychopathology, or psychological assessment Areas of clinical practice and theoretical orientation are open. Working Environment Bryant University is on a 465-acre campus in Smithfield, RI, 15 minutes from Providence, RI, and 45 minutes from Boston, MA. Throughout its more than 150-year history, Bryant has earned a distinguished reputation for innovative academic programs and technology that are marketplace-driven and highly attuned to the emerging needs of industry and society. Bryant’s close-knit, student-centered community of scholars delivers challenging academic programs that integrate business and the arts and sciences, with an emphasis on real-world application and a global perspective. Abundant co-curricular opportunities, service-learning programs, internships, and practicums allow students to put theory into practice while building character and leadership skills. Bryant is recognized as a leader in international business. At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC01642 Open Date 09/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions If interested, please apply online and submit the following materials: cover letter, CV, teaching statement. With questions, contact the search chair, Christina Tortolani, PhD – ctortolani@bryant.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Research Statement Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4883": {
      "title": "Public Relations and Strategic Communication - Professional in Residence",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Public Relations and Strategic Communication - Professional in Residence Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Public Relations and Strategic Communication - Professional in Residence Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Public Relations and Strategic Communication - Professional in Residence Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Faculty Reports To Dean, College of Humanities and Social Sciences Position Summary The Department of Communication, Media, and Sports Industries at Bryant University invites applications for a full-time position as Professional in Residence in Public Relations and Strategic Communication to begin Spring 2027 or Fall 2027. This is a renewable, non-tenure-track appointment designed for an accomplished communication practitioner who is passionate about preparing the next generation of public relations and strategic communication professionals. We welcome candidates from a wide range of professional backgrounds and lived experiences. The successful candidate will bring applied professional expertise into the classroom, bridging theory and industry practice across public relations strategy, media relations, organizational crisis communication, and related areas of the field. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030 , redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities Job Duties The Professional in Residence will teach four courses per semester in the Communication program and contribute meaningfully to departmental and university service. Core teaching responsibilities will center on public relations strategy, media relations, and strategic communication, with additional courses shaped by the candidate’s areas of expertise, as well as courses assigned to meet departmental needs. The position also involves active engagement with recruitment efforts, program promotion, professional outreach, and industry partnership development. Specific Duties Teach four courses per semester in the Department of Communication and Language Studies, with a focus on public relations, strategic communication, and media relations. Develop and enhance course offerings to keep the curriculum aligned with current industry practices and emerging trends in the field. Model inclusive communication approaches that align with contemporary professional standards in public relations and strategic communication. Advise and mentor students on academic planning, career pathways, and professional development in public relations and strategic communication. Provide service to the Department of Communication and Language Studies and Bryant University, including participation in departmental meetings, committees, and governance activities. Help facilitate open houses, information sessions, and recruitment events both on and off campus to attract future Public Relations focused students to the program. Maintain and develop active industry connections to support student internship and career placement opportunities. Collaborate with faculty on curriculum development, experiential learning initiatives, and department programming. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Potential candidates should, at a minimum, hold a master’s degree in Communication, Public Relations, or a related field; or possess an equivalent level of substantial professional experience in the industry. Candidates should also have a meaningful record of professional practice in public relations and/or strategic communication. We are looking for enthusiastic candidates who will inspire students, bring an impact‑focused approach, promote our programs, and have a positive impact on enrollment. We welcome applicants who are committed to fostering an inclusive, equitable learning environment; supporting students from diverse backgrounds; and contributing to a collaborative departmental culture. Additional qualifications are listed on Bryant University’s employment page linked below. Desired Qualifications Demonstrated professional experience in public relations, strategic communication, or a closely related field, with a strong network of industry contacts. Expertise in media relations, PR campaign strategy, social media management, and data-driven communication. Familiarity with emerging technologies and AI tools reshaping the public relations industry, including content creation strategy, digital messaging, and analytics. Accreditation in Public Relations ( APR ) preferred. Background in risk and/or crisis communication, including experience managing organizational reputation during high-stakes or sensitive public situations, is a plus. Experience in sports communication, public relations within professional or collegiate athletic contexts, or media relations in the sports industry is a plus. Teaching, public speaking, professional mentoring, training, or other related “educational leadership” experience desired but not required. Applying for the Position Candidates should provide academic transcripts or documentation of equivalent professional credentials, a current vitae or resume, and a letter of application that speaks to professional practice and experience. Candidates should also be prepared to provide two references upon request. Applicants are also encouraged to submit a brief teaching statement summarizing instructional experience, course offerings they are prepared to teach, and their approach to mentoring students in a professional communication program. The review of applications will begin immediately, and the position will remain open until filled. Find out more about us at: https://www.bryant.edu/undergraduate/academics/academic-departments/communication-and-language-studies-department For any further information, please contact Julie Volkman, Communication Search Chair, jvolkman@bryant.edu. Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC01636 Open Date 04/01/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Teaching Evaluation(s) Licenses and Certifications Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4881": {
      "title": "Professional in Residence for Applied Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Professional in Residence for Applied Artificial Intelligence Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Professional in Residence for Applied Artificial Intelligence Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To receive full consideration, interested individuals must apply electronically. To receive full consideration, applicants should submit: A letter of application describing interest in the position and relevant experience A current curriculum vitae If the applicant has teaching experience in higher education or professional environments, teaching evaluations, syllabi, and related materials. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Professional in Residence for Applied Artificial Intelligence Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Faculty Reports To Dean, College of Business Position Summary Bryant University seeks to fill three (3) full-time, Professional-in-Residence positions in Applied Artificial Intelligence. These positions are part of a strategic cluster hire to continue the expansion of our Applied AI curriculum, as well as the build-out of the Center for Applied AI. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching excellence and will play a central role in delivering undergraduate instruction in artificial intelligence. Should you wish to discuss this opening or request more information please contact Dr. Todd Alesandri, Dean of the College of Business. Bryant’s comprehensive and intentional approach to integration of AI can be found at https://www.bryant.edu/discover-bryant/ai-bryant. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030 , redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities The standard teaching load for this position is 6 courses per year, accompanied with additional responsibilities related to the Center for Applied AI. Primary teaching responsibilities will include introductory and applied AI courses, but may also include selected upper-level electives in Artificial Intelligence, Generative AI, and emerging AI applications as program needs evolve. The position is intended for individuals with professional experience and a strong applied orientation—someone who can translate AI concepts into accessible, hands-on learning experiences for primarily undergraduate students across business and related disciplines. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Master’s degree or higher in Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Information Systems, Computer Science, Analytics, or a closely related field. Ability to design and teach hands-on AI and data analytics projects. Demonstrated experience in applying AI in at least one of several domains, such as accounting, finance, marketing, healthcare, insurance or media. Strong communication skills and the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences. Knowledge of responsible AI practices, including ethical considerations in AI deployment. Preferred Qualifications: Prior college-level teaching experience would be beneficial but not necessary. Professional or applied experience working with AI Application Development, AI tools, AI platforms, or AI-enabled workflows. Familiarity with generative AI technologies, prompt engineering, and AI applications in business or organizational settings. Bryant University provides an inclusive and welcoming educational and working environments for all members of its community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual preference or orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, ethnicity, disability, genetic information, protected veteran, or marital status. Working Environment Bryant University is a 163-year-old private institution that is accredited by AACSB -International and the New England Commission of Higher Education ( NECHE ). Bryant is a student-centered institution, dedicated to educating and inspiring students to discover their passion, become innovative leaders with character, and make a difference around the world. Our innovative academic programs are attuned to the needs of industry and society with a strong commitment to experiential learning. We have approximately 3,200 undergraduate students from 38 states and 42 countries. We also have approximately 400 full- and part-time graduate students. At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC01633 Open Date 03/17/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Applicant Special Instructions To receive full consideration, interested individuals must apply electronically. To receive full consideration, applicants should submit: A letter of application describing interest in the position and relevant experience A current curriculum vitae If the applicant has teaching experience in higher education or professional environments, teaching evaluations, syllabi, and related materials. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Teaching Evaluation(s) Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4880": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Associate Professor of Finance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Associate Professor of Finance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To receive full consideration, interested individuals must apply electronically. Applications should include a letter of application, current vita, and evidence of the following: Excellence in teaching undergraduate and graduate finance courses. Published research in high quality finance journals. Service to the university and community including the development of new courses or program leadership. Contributions to student growth and development through active involvement in student related activities (e.g., advising, working with student organizations). Complete information regarding the required application process is available on-line at https://employment.bryant.edu/ Bryant University will begin reviewing applications immediately and will be conducting initial interviews both on campus and via teleconference. Should you wish to discuss this opening or request more information, please contact Dr. Kevin Maloney, kmaloney2@bryant.edu , Chair of the Department of Finance. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Associate Professor of Finance Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Faculty Reports To Dean, College of Business Position Summary Bryant University seeks to hire an Associate Professor of Finance. Highly qualified candidates for an Assistant Professor position might also be considered. The successful candidate will have a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, to scholarly research, and to departmental and university service. While we welcome applications from candidates in all areas of finance, we have a particular need for a candidate with research and teaching interest in corporate finance and private equity. The successful candidate will teach in our undergraduate ( BSBA ) and graduate business programs. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030 , redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities Research Data Support Bryant subscribes to the typical databases used in financial research (e.g., CRSP , Compustat), plus a number of specialized data services in support of research on corporate governance, banking, and ESG topics. We utilize the WRDS platform at Bryant to organize these databases. Bryant also provides access to FactSet, Morningstar, and Bloomberg to support research and teaching in Finance in our state of the art Financial Markets Center. Appointment Rank is Associate Professor. Salary is commensurate with experience, demonstrated scholarly performance, and will be consistent with AACSB salary levels. The appointment would commence with the start of the 2027-2028 academic year. Candidates would be expected to apply for tenure within two years of employment at Bryant, depending on prior experience and their research accomplishments. A candidate with fewer years of experience could be considered for the rank of Assistant Professor, and the timing to a tenure decision would be longer. Bryant University provides an inclusive and welcoming educational and working environments for all members of its community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual preference or orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, ethnicity, disability, genetic information, protected veteran, or marital status. Qualifications Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Finance from an AACSB -International or EQUIS accredited institution. Candidates must have a demonstrated record of publications in high quality peer-reviewed journals. Research that speaks to both academic and managerial audiences is highly desirable. Candidates must have at least 6 years of teaching experience in a business school and experience teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels to qualify for the Associate Professor role. A highly qualified candidate with at least 3 years’ experience could be considered for an Assistant Professor role. Evidence of curricular innovation and a demonstrated commitment to service as an active member of a university community is also required. Successful candidates will also demonstrate they can design and lead new initiatives that support research and teaching, e.g., building innovative programs, authoring research grants, establishing connections with the business community and alumni, and developing new courses. Working Environment Bryant University is a 163-year-old private institution that is accredited by AACSB -International and the New England Commission of Higher Education ( NECHE ). Bryant is a student-centered institution, dedicated to educating and inspiring students to discover their passion, become innovative leaders with character, and make a difference around the world. Our innovative academic programs are attuned to the needs of industry and society with a strong commitment to experiential learning We have approximately 3,700 undergraduate students from 38 states and 40 countries. We also have approximately 400 full- and part-time graduate students. The Finance Department currently consists of ten tenured or tenure-track faculty members, six full-time non-tenure track faculty members, and several adjunct professors. Due to high student demand for our courses and programs, we are seeking to grow the size of the full-time Finance Department faculty. Students interested in Finance can earn concentrations in finance as part of our undergraduate degrees in business administration ( BSBA ) or international business ( BSIB ). We also offer a specialized concentration in financial services for undergraduate students, and we offer graduate courses in Finance as part of Master’s degree programs. Bryant does not have a doctoral program in Finance. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC01643 Open Date 10/05/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions To receive full consideration, interested individuals must apply electronically. Applications should include a letter of application, current vita, and evidence of the following: Excellence in teaching undergraduate and graduate finance courses. Published research in high quality finance journals. Service to the university and community including the development of new courses or program leadership. Contributions to student growth and development through active involvement in student related activities (e.g., advising, working with student organizations). Complete information regarding the required application process is available on-line at https://employment.bryant.edu/ Bryant University will begin reviewing applications immediately and will be conducting initial interviews both on campus and via teleconference. Should you wish to discuss this opening or request more information, please contact Dr. Kevin Maloney, kmaloney2@bryant.edu , Chair of the Department of Finance. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Teaching Evaluation(s) Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4876": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Department of Information Systems and Analytics",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Lecturer, Department of Information Systems and Analytics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Lecturer, Department of Information Systems and Analytics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Lecturer, Department of Information Systems and Analytics Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Faculty Reports To Dean, College of Business Position Summary The Department of Information Systems and Analytics ( ISA ) at Bryant University invites applications for a lecturer, for the Spring semester beginning January 19, 2027, to May 4, 2027. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to our undergraduate and graduate ISA programs in IS, Data Science, Business Analytics and Applied AI. We especially welcome applicants qualified to teach courses in IT Infrastructure and Cloud Computing, Cybersecurity, and IT Security and Risk Management. Candidates with additional expertise in Artificial Intelligence and Robotics are preferred. This position requires a strong commitment to teaching excellence. In addition, the position requires contribution to occasional service projects at the department, college, and university level. Salary is market based and commensurate with preparation, experience, and demonstrated performance. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030 , redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Bryant University’s ISA Department consists of nine tenure-track faculty and one non- tenure track faculty members who bring extensive business experience to the classroom. We offer various programs in IS, Data Science, Business Analytics and Applied AI at both undergraduate and graduate levels. Principal Accountabilities Teach undergraduate courses in IT Infrastructure and Cloud Computing, Cybersecurity and related courses. Develop and deliver course materials that integrate current industry practices, cloud platforms, cybersecurity frameworks, and emerging AI applications. Contribute to the development and accreditation of the ISA curriculum through service activities at the departmental, college, and university levels. Collaborate with other faculty and mentor Bryant students to enhance learning community and outcomes. Build and maintain connections with the business community to support experiential learning and student success. Serve as an active member of the Bryant University community. Qualifications Master’s degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Information Technology, Data Science, or a closely related field from an AACSB -accredited institution (or equivalent accreditation) Significant professional experience in cybersecurity, IT infrastructure, cloud computing, or related fields. Demonstrated teaching effectiveness at the university level. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Ability to teach introductory courses in Artificial Intelligence. Experience with hands-on, lab-based, or experiential learning approaches. Working knowledge of robotics systems and experience developing applications for humanoid robots. Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC01630 Open Date 03/10/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Teaching Evaluation(s) Licenses and Certifications Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
