    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4874": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach - Women’s Club Lacrosse",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Coach - Women’s Club Lacrosse Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Assistant Coach - Women’s Club Lacrosse Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Coach - Women’s Club Lacrosse Full Time / Part Time Part Time Job Type Staff Reports To Head Coach, Women's Club Lacrosse Position Summary Bryant University is hiring for a part-time Assistant Coach for Women’s Club Lacrosse. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030, redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities Assistant with direct responsibility of the Women’s Club Lacrosse Program Direct one or more division area(s) (i.e. A/B teams), as assigned Assist with scheduling, planning, attending, and implementing all practices and matches in a professional and ethical manner Communicate effectively and serve as a mentor and coach with student athletes so that student athletes develop their full potential as individuals and athletes Assist other coaches and team members in fundraising efforts, alumnae development, and serve as point person for some initiatives. Assist with the design and implementation of the on-campus recruiting strategy for novice players. Qualifications Must be First Aid/ CPR / AED certified. Must have extensive understanding of lacrosse rules and strategy Must have previous experience playing and/or coaching the sport of lacrosse Preferably experience and extensive knowledge with offensive strategies This is a part-time paid position. The compensation is commensurate with experience Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number STA02833 Work Hours Days/Hours: Weekday afternoons & evenings, weekends Open Date 09/18/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Multi Media Letter(s) of Recommendation Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
