      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Teaching Opportunities - Finance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Adjunct Teaching Opportunities - Finance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To receive full consideration, interested individuals should send an email to Kevin Maloney, Chair of the Finance Department at Bryant, kmaloney2@bryant.edu . Please include a resume or curriculum vita and teaching evaluations if you have taught in the past. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Teaching Opportunities - Finance Full Time / Part Time Part Time Job Type Adjunct Reports To Dean, College of Business Position Summary Bryant University is seeking an Adjunct Professor of Finance for the Spring 2027 semester. The successful candidate will have a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and to bringing their experience to the classroom. We have a particular need for an individual who could teach one or two of the following undergraduate courses: Financial Management, Financial Institutions and Markets, Intermediate Corporate Finance, Financial Statement Analysis, or Real Estate Finance. Descriptions of these courses can be accessed via the Course Catalogue on the Bryant website. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030 , redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities This position includes teaching at the undergraduate level as well as contributing to student growth and development through active involvement in student related co-curricular activities. Qualifications Candidates must have at least a Master’s Degree in Finance or a related field from an AACSB -International or EQUIS accredited institution. Relevant industry or regulatory experience in finance or prior teaching experience at a business school is required. Working Environment Bryant University provides an inclusive and welcoming educational and working environment for all members of its community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual preference or orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, ethnicity, disability, genetic information, protected veteran, or marital status. Bryant University is a 163-year-old private institution that is accredited by AACSB -International and the New England Commission of Higher Education ( NECHE ). Bryant is a student-centered institution, dedicated to educating and inspiring students to discover their passion, become innovative leaders with character, and make a difference around the world. Our innovative academic programs are attuned to the needs of industry and society with a strong commitment to experiential learning. We have approximately 3,600 undergraduate students from 38 states and 40 countries. We also have approximately 400 full- and part-time graduate students. At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive 