    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4871": {
      "title": "Director, Advancement Content &amp; Stewardship",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Director, Advancement Content &amp; Stewardship Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Director, Advancement Content & Stewardship Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Director, Advancement Content & Stewardship Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Staff Reports To Associate Vice President, Development Operations Position Summary The Director of Advancement Content & Stewardship leads strategic communications, donor stewardship, and content development in support of Bryant University’s fundraising, campaign, and engagement priorities. Reporting to the Associate Vice President, Development Operations, The Director oversees the development and delivery of fundraising proposals, cases for support, donor impact reports, stewardship communications, campaign materials, executive presentations, and other strategic donor-facing communications. Serving as the primary liaison between University Advancement (UA) and University Marketing & Communications ( UMC ), the Director manages Advancement communications strategy, project execution, and stakeholder collaboration while ensuring Advancement communications align with institutional priorities, fundraising objectives, and University brand standards. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030, redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities 40% Advancement Content, Fundraising Communications & Stewardship Lead the development of integrated fundraising, campaign, and stewardship communications supporting annual, leadership, major, principal gift, and campaign priorities. Partner with University Marketing & Communications to align Advancement campaign messaging, fundraising communications, and donor engagement strategies with institutional priorities, University brand standards and established messaging frameworks. Serve as the primary communications partner to Advancement leadership and gift officers, developing donor-centered messaging in collaboration with University Marketing & Communications and other campus partners as appropriate. Oversee the creation of proposals, cases for support, donor impact reports, campaign materials, donor presentations, and other strategic communications. Partner with campus stakeholders to identify philanthropic priorities, funding opportunities, and impact stories that demonstrate the value of donor support. Promote philanthropy through impactful storytelling, donor recognition communications, and stewardship initiatives that strengthen donor engagement and retention. 25% Project Management & Stakeholder Coordination Serve as the primary project manager for Advancement communications and stewardship initiatives, overseeing Advancement planning, prioritization, content development, stakeholder coordination, review processes, execution, and delivery. Serve as the primary Advancement point of contact with University Marketing and Communications, providing complete project briefs and coordinating with appropriate UMC functional leads to facilitate creative, communications, and production needs. Partner with UMC project leads to establish timelines, deliverables, responsibilities, and communication cadence for the UMC components of Advancement projects. Coordinate Advancement content development, stakeholder reviews, approvals, and communication cadence among Advancement, University partners, University Marketing & Communications, and external vendors, serving as the primary Advancement point of contact for projects requiring UMC support Develop and maintain Advancement project management tools, content calendars, workflows, and reporting mechanisms that improve efficiency and accountability. Ensure communication activities are documented within the Advancement CRM system and identify opportunities to improve processes, resource allocation, and project execution. 15% Donor Impact, Recognition & Stewardship Programs Lead the development and implementation of donor stewardship, impact-reporting, and recognition strategies that strengthen donor relationships and retention. Oversee donor impact reports, beneficiary stories, stewardship reports, and related donor communications. Partner with Development, Donor Experience, Annual Giving, Alumni Engagement, and campus stakeholders to communicate the outcomes of philanthropic support. Create opportunities for donor engagement and recognition that demonstrate the impact of philanthropy and strengthen connections to the University. 10% Multimedia & Executive Communications Lead the planning, content development, messaging strategy, and coordination of photography, video, multimedia, and storytelling initiatives within Advancement, partnering with University Marketing & Communications and external vendors as appropriate to support production and execution. Develop executive presentations, donor-facing materials, and strategic communications supporting Advancement priorities for trustees, campaign volunteers, senior leaders, prospects, donors, and other key stakeholders; collaborate with University Marketing & Communications and external partners as appropriate to ensure alignment with institutional priorities and brand standards. Leverage emerging technologies and industry best practices to enhance content development, operational efficiency, donor engagement, and communications effectiveness. 10% Staff Leadership & Team Development Lead and develop Advancement Communications and Stewardship staff, providing strategic oversight for communications, donor stewardship, donor recognition, and impact-reporting initiatives. Establish goals, manage performance, and provide coaching and professional development that promotes accountability, collaboration, and innovation. Promote a collaborative, high-performing culture and consistent communications and project management practices. Perform other duties as assigned in support of University Advancement priorities and Bryant University’s Vision 2030 goals. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required, with 6-8 years of progressively responsible experience in advancement communications, fundraising communications, donor stewardship, content strategy, project management, marketing communications, or a related field; higher education experience preferred. The successful candidate will demonstrate exceptional writing, editing, communication, and project management skills; experience developing fundraising and stewardship communications; and the ability to manage complex projects, build collaborative partnerships, work effectively across stakeholder groups, and lead staff. Experience managing communications initiatives involving multiple stakeholders, review processes, and shared decision-making responsibilities is preferred. Experience with CRM systems, fundraising databases, digital media platforms, design software, project management tools, artificial intelligence applications, and other advancement technologies is preferred. Evening and weekend work may be required, and travel may be necessary. Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number STA02831 Work Hours Open Date 09/28/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please briefly describe your experience developing donor-facing communications, such as proposals, cases for support, impact reports, stewardship materials, or campaign communications. (Open Ended Question) * Tell us about a communications or stewardship project you led from concept through completion. What was your role, and what made the project successful? (Open Ended Question) * This role works with senior leaders, fundraisers, donors, and campus partners to translate complex ideas into compelling communications. Please share an example of how you have adapted content or messaging for different audiences. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4870": {
      "title": "Adjunct Teaching Opportunities - Information Systems and Analytics",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Teaching Opportunities - Information Systems and Analytics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Adjunct Teaching Opportunities - Information Systems and Analytics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Teaching Opportunities - Information Systems and Analytics Full Time / Part Time Part Time Job Type Adjunct Reports To Chair, Information Systems and Analytics Position Summary The Department of Information Systems and Analytics at Bryant University invites applications for adjunct instructors to teach the following courses: AA630 Data Management and Visualization Monday between 6:30pm and 9:10pm ISA310 Data Visualization Monday and Thursday between 5:30pm and 6:45pm ISA472 IT Security and Risk Management Monday and Thursday between 2:20pm and 3:35pm In addition to the specific course section listed above, the Department of ISA is also seeking to build a qualified pool of adjunct instructors who may be available to teach a range of undergraduate courses during the spring 2027 semester. We welcome applications from experienced IT, Analytics and Data Science professionals and educators with expertise in areas such as cybersecurity, Analytics and AI. Candidates who are interested in being considered for future course assignments are encouraged to apply, noting their areas of specialization and availability. Course Descriptions: AA630 Data Management and Visualization This course equips students with practical skills and knowledge in managing and manipulating data using Python and SQL , two of the most essential tools in modern analytics. Students will gain an in-depth understanding of relational databases, including schema design, normalization, and query optimization. They will learn to write efficient SQL queries for extracting, transforming, and analyzing data from databases, applying advanced techniques such as joins, subqueries, and aggregations. The Python component of the course focuses on importing, cleaning, transforming, and summarizing data for analysis. Students will work with real-world datasets, applying Python libraries like pandas and numpy to handle data preprocessing and manipulation tasks. Emphasis will be placed on building seamless workflows that integrate Python and SQL for end-to-end data management solutions. Through practical assignments and a project, students will apply their skills to solve data management challenges, demonstrating their ability to handle complex datasets and provide actionable insights. This course prepares students to manage data workflows efficiently and apply their skills in business analytics, decision-making, and data-driven environments. AA310 Data Visualization This course examines the art and science of data visualization with a central emphasis on storytelling with data. Beyond the mechanics of plotting points and generating charts, the course highlights how visualizations can be woven into coherent stories that engage audiences and drive action. We will explore how storytelling principles—such as context, narrative flow, emphasis, and clarity—interact with visualization design to shape the way information is perceived and remembered. By studying how elements such as shape, size, color, orientation, and motion influence comprehension, students will learn to craft visualizations that not only present information clearly but also communicate a compelling story that connects data to insight. ISA472 IT Security and Risk Management This course explores IT Security from the perspective of risk management. Assessment of IT systems is critical to developing strategies to mitigate and manage risks. This course focuses on effective assessment and risk management strategies that ultimately help the student to implement effective and proactive risk mitigation measures and risk management practices. This course focuses on the IT security threat environment, cryptography, securing networks, access control, firewalls, host hardening, application security, data protections, incident response, and policy. A clear theoretical understanding supports a practical component. Students will learn to audit information systems and use contemporary security software. Hands’ on labs are assigned to simulate risk management processes. Principal Accountabilities This position includes teaching at the undergraduate level as well as contributing to student growth and development through active involvement in student related co-curricular activities. Qualifications Qualified candidates should hold a master’s degree in a relevant field. Candidates should also have foundational knowledge of information technology management, proficiency with Microsoft Excel, and basic programming skills. Certain requirements are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate persons with disabilities Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number ADJ01610 Work Hours Open Date 09/29/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Teaching Evaluation(s) Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4869": {
      "title": "Stewardship Associate",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Stewardship Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Stewardship Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Stewardship Associate Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Staff Reports To Director, Advancement Communications and Stewardship Position Summary Reporting to the Director, Advancement Communications and Stewardship, the Stewardship Associate supports the execution of donor stewardship activities that foster donor engagement, recognition, and accountability. Working collaboratively with Development, Annual Giving, Donor Experience, Advancement Communications, and campus partners, the position coordinates stewardship communications, scholarship reporting, donor recognition initiatives, and student engagement activities that demonstrate the impact of philanthropic support and support meaningful donor experiences. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030, redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities 35% Stewardship Communications & Donor Recognition Coordinate recurring stewardship activities, including first-time donor acknowledgements, tribute and memorial gift stewardship, leadership society recognition, and other donor recognition initiatives. Assist in the development and distribution of stewardship communications, donor impact reports, scholarship reports, stewardship correspondence, and related materials. Partner with the Advancement Content & Stewardship team to maintain stewardship templates, recognition materials, and communication resources. Monitor stewardship processes to ensure communications are accurate, timely, and aligned with donor recognition standards. 30% Student Engagement, Scholarship Reporting & Content Collection Coordinate annual scholarship reporting and related stewardship activities for donors outside of Tier 1 and Tier 2 giving levels. Coordinate annual scholarship reporting for donors outside of Tier 1 and Tier 2 giving levels. Collect and manage student-generated content, including thank-you messages, testimonials, photos, and stories, for use in scholarship reports and stewardship communications. Coordinate student participation in stewardship initiatives, including Thank a Donor Day and other donor gratitude programs. 25% Stewardship Events & Program Support Coordinate stewardship-focused events and engagement opportunities, including donor recognition activities, scholarship events, and donor-student engagement programs. Lead the planning and execution of donor gratitude initiatives, including Thank-a-Donor programs and similar stewardship activities. Partner with Donor Experience and Development colleagues to support stewardship components of donor events and recognition programs. Assist with stewardship initiatives supporting annual donors, leadership donors, scholarship donors, athletics supporters, and other key donor constituencies. 10% Administrative Support & Collaboration Maintain stewardship tracking systems, reports, and related records within the Advancement CRM . Collaborate with colleagues across University Advancement to support consistent donor stewardship, impact reporting, and recognition efforts. Perform other duties as assigned Certain requirements are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate persons with disabilities Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and 2-4 years of relevant professional experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Higher education experience preferred. Strong organizational, communication, project management, and relationship-building skills are required. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications is required; experience with fundraising databases and CRM systems is preferred. Flexibility to work occasional evenings and weekends may be required. Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number STA02832 Work Hours Open Date 09/28/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
