    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4852": {
      "title": "Major Gift Officer",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Major Gift Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Major Gift Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Major Gift Officer Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Staff Reports To Assistant Vice President, Development Position Summary This position is accountable for the identification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of individual donors among Bryant’s alumni, parents, and friends. The ability of the officer to engage potential contributors, determine their interests and match them to the needs of the University, and assist these individuals in making gifts of $25,000 or more, will be critical to Bryant’s success in the coming years. While local candidates are encouraged to apply, qualified applicants residing in Maryland or Florida will also be considered for remote work . Bryant University is a private New England university with a tradition of innovation and a global vision for success. Our new strategic plan, Vision 2030 , sets a trajectory for the next decade through academic excellence, outstanding student life, competitive athletics and student outcomes among the nation’s top 1% for ROI . Principal Accountabilities Under the direction of the Assistant Vice President, Development, the Major Gift Officer is responsible for the design and implementation of a strategic annual plan focused on identifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding alumni, parent and friend leadership giving prospects within their assigned prospect portfolio (200 prospects including alumni, parents and friends of the University), through personal visits, correspondence, attendance at cultivation events, etc. Requires regular travel to manage portfolio of assigned prospects. Participate in developing appropriate prospect cultivation strategies, determining potential giving opportunities and optimal gift levels; provide regular reports of all activities through designated reporting methods and inputting information in Development’s database. Meet assigned goals for prospect visits and dollars to be raised, as well as other performance metrics, to be determined annually. Recruit and manage assigned volunteers and assist them in their fund-raising assignments. Maintain knowledge of planned giving arrangements, pertinent tax laws and other factors that will impact and facilitate donors’ ability to make substantial gifts. Collaborate closely with Bryant’s Planned Giving Officer to ensure prospects are able to achieve their philanthropic goals though planned and/or blended gift options. Effectively motivate and collaborate with staff to work as a team in meeting all individual and Departmental goals and ensuring that practices are in compliance with the spirit and intent of the University’s policy on diversity and EEO /AA guidelines. Perform related duties as assigned. Qualifications This position is best filled by an individual with an undergraduate degree, advanced degree preferred; 7 – 10 years of demonstrated success in fund raising and capital campaigns, preferably in a higher education setting; experience in recruiting, motivating and managing volunteers in successful fund raising efforts; knowledge of and success in devising blended and planned gift solicitations; ability to plan and think strategically; detail-oriented, but able to manage multiple projects simultaneously; strong interpersonal, writing and communications skills. Requires a proven track record is soliciting major gifts of $25,000 or more. Microsoft Office Suite and CRM Advance experience is a plus. Certain requirements are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate persons with disabilities. Travel and non-standard hour are required. Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number STA02697 Work Hours This is a full-time position with competitive salary and excellent benefits. While local candidates are encouraged to apply, qualified applicants residing in Maryland or Florida will also be considered for remote work . Open Date 05/29/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4849": {
      "title": "Student Support &amp; Response Coordinator",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Student Support &amp; Response Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Student Support & Response Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Student Support & Response Coordinator Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Staff Reports To Associate Vice President of Community & Belonging Position Summary The Student Support & Response Coordinator provides case management, administrative, and programmatic support for University processes related to Title IX, bias incidents, and student leaves of absence. Reporting to the Associate Vice President of Community & Belonging, the Student Support & Response Coordinator works closely with the Title IX Coordinator, Bias Incident Committee, Student Affairs, and other campus partners to ensure students receive timely, coordinated, and compassionate support while University policies and procedures are administered consistently and effectively. The Student Support & Response Coordinator serves as an important point of connection for students navigating sensitive or complex circumstances. The position coordinates communications, meetings, documentation, referrals, and follow-up; maintains accurate and confidential records; and helps students understand available resources, options, and next steps. This position may required non-standard work hours including nights and weekends. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030, redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities Title IX Office Support Provide administrative and case management support to the Title IX Coordinator on reports involving sex discrimination, sexual harassment, sexual misconduct, relationship violence, stalking, and other concerns addressed under University policy. Receive and respond to reports and inquiries involving potential Title IX concerns and facilitate appropriate follow-up and referral. Assist individuals in understanding the University’s Title IX process, reporting options, supportive measures, and available resources. Coordinate meetings between the Title IX Coordinator and students, advisors, employees, and other involved parties. Assist with intake processes and ensure appropriate documentation and information are collected and maintained. Coordinate and track supportive measures, including academic, housing, employment, safety, and other accommodations, in partnership with appropriate University offices. Prepare routine correspondence, notices, meeting materials, and other case-related documentation under the direction of the Title IX Coordinator. Maintain case files and case management systems and monitor deadlines, required follow-up, and case milestones. Provide students with information about campus and community resources and facilitate referrals when appropriate. Assist the Title IX Coordinator with educational programs, prevention initiatives, communications, and other Title IX compliance activities. Support the collection and organization of information needed for institutional reporting, trend analysis, and assessment. Maintain strict confidentiality and appropriately handle highly sensitive student information. Bias Incident Committee Support Provide administrative and case coordination support to the University’s Bias Incident Committee and its leadership. Receive and appropriately route reports of potential bias incidents in accordance with University procedures. Coordinate intake meetings and follow-up conversations with students and other members of the University community. Maintain confidential records of reported incidents, actions taken, referrals, and case outcomes. Track cases to ensure timely review, communication, and follow-up. Assist individuals in understanding the University’s bias incident process and available support resources. Coordinate referrals to appropriate University departments as needed. Prepare meeting agendas, case summaries, correspondence, and other materials for committee review. Support the identification and analysis of trends in reported incidents to inform education, prevention, and campus climate initiatives. Assist with educational programming, communications, and resources designed to promote an inclusive and respectful campus environment. Student Leave Management and Return-to-Campus Support Coordinate the administrative process for student leaves of absence, including personal, medical, and other applicable leave categories. Serve as a primary resource for students considering or requesting a leave, helping them understand the process, requirements, timelines, and potential implications. Guide students through required documentation and approvals and coordinate with appropriate campus offices to facilitate the leave process. Maintain accurate and confidential records of student leaves and monitor relevant deadlines and follow-up requirements. Communicate with students throughout the leave process to ensure they understand their status and next steps. Coordinate with Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, Financial Aid, the Registrar, Residence Life, Counseling Services, Health Services, and other University offices as appropriate. Support students preparing to return from leave by coordinating required documentation, approvals, resources, and transition planning. Help identify barriers that may affect a student’s successful return and connect students with appropriate University resources. Track leave and return trends and assist in evaluating opportunities to improve processes and the student experience. Ensure leave practices are administered consistently and in accordance with University policies and applicable requirements. General Case Management, Records, and Process Improvement Maintain organized, accurate, timely, and confidential case records across assigned areas of responsibility. Develop and maintain tracking systems for cases, deadlines, communications, referrals, and outcomes. Identify cases requiring escalation and promptly bring significant or time-sensitive concerns to appropriate University leadership. Facilitate coordination among University offices when a student’s circumstances involve multiple areas of support. Assist in reviewing and improving policies, procedures, forms, communications, and workflows related to assigned responsibilities. Develop reports and summaries that identify trends, service needs, process gaps, and opportunities for prevention or improvement. Maintain current knowledge of relevant University policies and applicable federal and state requirements. Participate in professional development and training related to Title IX, bias response, student support, case management, and leave administration. Perform other related duties as assigned. Certain requirements are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate individuals with disabilities. Qualifications QUALITIES & CHARACTERISTICS : High degree of professionalism with the ability to accurately maintain confidential information and records. Comfort working both independently and collaboratively in situations that may require consultation, judgement, and timely action. Empathy and professionalism when interacting with individuals experiencing challenging circumstances. Ability to interpret and consistently apply policies and established procedures. Exceptional discretion and sound judgement when handling sensitive matters. An ability to build trust and productive relationships across the University. Strong organizational skills, including the ability to manage multiple deadlines and priorities simultaneously. Strong attention to detail and documentation. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Open and responsive to direction and feedback. QUALIFICATIONS & TRAINING : This position is best served by an individual with: Bachelor’s degree in higher education, student affairs, human resources, social sciences, counseling, legal studies, or a related field. Minimum of three years of relevant professional experience in higher education, student affairs, human resources, compliance, case management, student support, or a related area. Knowledge of Title IX, FERPA , ADA /Section 504, and other laws and regulations relevant to higher education student support. Experience supporting Title IX, student conduct, bias response, student care, or related processes is preferred. Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number STA02826 Work Hours Open Date 09/11/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4841": {
      "title": "Director, Center for Applied Artificial Intelligence/ Faculty Program Director",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Director, Center for Applied Artificial Intelligence/ Faculty Program Director Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Director, Center for Applied Artificial Intelligence/ Faculty Program Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Director, Center for Applied Artificial Intelligence/ Faculty Program Director Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Staff Reports To Provost & Chief Academic Officer Position Summary Reporting to the Provost & Chief Academic Officer, the Director provides strategic, academic, and operational leadership for Bryant University’s Center for Applied Artificial Intelligence (the “Center”). The Director translates Bryant’s AI vision into practice by strengthening AI-infused education and credentials, expanding applied research and external partnerships, and promoting the responsible, ethical, and secure use of AI across the University. The Center operates in a hub-and-spoke model. As the institutional “hub” leader, the Director coordinates with cross-campus partners—particularly deans and program directors, the Center for Teaching Excellence, the Sprague Center for Entrepreneurship and Design Thinking, the Sales Institute, the Executive Education & Career Accelerator, and the Office of Information Services—to ensure that Bryant’s AI strategy is integrated, scalable, and measurable. Key partners and stakeholders Provost, deans, academic leaders, and faculty across Bryant’s colleges Center for Teaching Excellence (faculty development, pedagogy, course design) Sprague Center for Entrepreneurship and Design Thinking (programming, prototyping, venture support) Bryant University Sales Institute and the Hauck Sales Performance Lab (experiential learning, competitions, employer engagement) Executive Education & Career Accelerator (certificates, corporate training, revenue-generating programs) Office of Information Services (data governance, privacy and security, platforms, IT enablement) University Advancement (fundraising strategy, stewardship, and impact reporting) Corporate and community partners (workforce readiness, internships, employer engagement) This position may be appointed as either a Staff Director or a Faculty Director. The specific appointment will be based on the selected candidate’s qualifications, academic preparation, and relevant experience. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030, redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities Core responsibilities aligned with the Center’s pillars: Strategic leadership and operations Set and execute a multi-year strategy for the Center; build annual operating plans, priorities, and measurable outcomes. Provide operational leadership for Center’s staffing, budgeting, reporting, policy development, vendor relationships, and continuous improvement. Recruit, support, and evaluate Center personnel—including the program manager, other staff, and student fellows—and convene advisory structures as needed. Serve as the Center’s primary spokesperson and convener for AI initiatives—internally and externally. Hub-and-spoke integration and campus partnership leadership Curricular integration (deans and program directors): Support and facilitate the development and evaluation of AI-infused curricular pathways, stackable credentials, and experiential learning projects across disciplines. Pedagogy ( CTE ): Partner to design faculty development offerings on AI-enabled teaching, assessment integrity, and the responsible use of educational technology; align Center programming with faculty needs. Innovation and venture creation (Sprague Center): Connect AI to design thinking, makerspace prototyping, and entrepreneurship programming; support venture, product, and service concepts that leverage AI. Workforce and corporate upskilling (Executive Education & Career Accelerator): Develop and scale certificates and customized training programs, such as foundational and role-based AI programs, that address workforce needs and enhance Bryant’s regional visibility. Experiential learning: Support the colleges and the Sales Institute in developing and expanding AI-focused internships, corporate projects, student competitions, and hackathons. Maintain a regular cadence of planning with campus partners to ensure alignment, resourcing, and shared accountability. Faculty innovation and applied scholarship Support CTE and academic leaders in advancing faculty innovation through seed grants, course redesign support, interdisciplinary project teams, and applied research collaborations with external partners. Build communities of practice that elevate ethical, human-centered AI, verification, and critical thinking across disciplines. Corporate and community partnerships Develop a grant-funded AI Accelerator within the Center to provide training and consulting services to small businesses in Rhode Island. This work will be conducted in close collaboration with the Executive Education & Career Accelerator and the John H. Chafee Center for International Business. The Director will devote a significant portion of time to this initiative during the first two years. Cultivate and manage industry relationships that generate internships, project-based learning, datasets, scholarships, and applied pilots. Qualifications Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number STA02823 Work Hours Open Date 08/25/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
