    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4840": {
      "title": "Development Officer",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Development Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Development Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Development Officer Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Staff Reports To Assistant Vice President, Development Position Summary This position is accountable for the identification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of prospects including Bryant’s alumni, parents, and friends. The Development Officer will maintain a portfolio of leadership ($1,000 – $24,999) donors and prospects to identify, cultivate, solicit and steward in their philanthropic support of the University and help build a pipeline of major and planned gift prospects using a combination of in-person and virtual visits combined with email, social media, video, and text message. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030, redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities Manage a pool of 1,000+ assigned leadership-level ($1,000-$24,000) gift prospects serving as the primary Bryant contact leveraging both multi-channel digital (social media, email, video conferencing) and face-to-face contact (personal visits, attendance at cultivation events, etc.). The Officer will build collaborative, trusting relationships with prospects, donors, and volunteers and ensure that each has a clear strategy and timeline for cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship. Participate in developing appropriate multi-channel prospect cultivation strategies, determining potential giving opportunities and optimal gift levels; provide regular reports of all activities through designated reporting methods and inputting information in Development database. Meet assigned goals for prospect contacts and dollars to be raised as determined annually. Work closely with colleagues in other areas of University Advancement (Bryant Fund, Major Gifts, Advancement Services, Communication and Stewardship) to ensure donors are moved along in the gift giving pipeline. Perform related duties as assigned. Qualifications This position is best filled by an individual with an undergraduate degree, advanced degree preferred; at least 1-3 years of demonstrated success in fundraising. Experience in digital fundraising and/or digital marketing to create highly personalized communications and in a Higher Education setting is a plus. The Officer must be able to plan and think strategically; be detail-oriented, but able to manage multiple projects simultaneously; and have strong interpersonal, writing and communications skills. Microsoft Office Suite and Razor’s Edge NXT Database experience is a plus. Certain requirements are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate persons with disabilities. Travel and non-standard hour are required. Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number STA02822 Work Hours Open Date 08/27/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
