    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4904": {
      "title": "Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty position (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Politics, Law and Society",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty position (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Politics, Law and Society Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty position (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Politics, Law and Society Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty position (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Politics, Law and Society Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Faculty Reports To Dean, College of Humanities and Social Sciences Position Summary The Department of Politics, Law and Society at Bryant University invites applications for a Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty position (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor). The successful candidate must demonstrate strong teaching ability in either Introduction to U.S. Politics or Introduction to International Politics, with preference given to candidates who can teach both introductory courses. Additional teaching opportunities include upper-level courses in the discipline and the University’s interdisciplinary General Education Capstone. Rank will be determined based on the candidate’s academic preparation, qualifications, and experience. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030 , redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities Teach undergraduate courses in Introduction to U.S. Politics, Introduction to International Politics, upper-level political science courses, and the interdisciplinary General Education Capstone, as appropriate. Develop and deliver engaging course materials that promote critical thinking, student engagement, and achievement of learning outcomes. Integrate relevant artificial intelligence (AI) concepts and applications into teaching to enhance student learning and support responsible use of emerging technologies. Collaborate with departmental colleagues to support curriculum development, instructional excellence, and student success. Participate in departmental and university service activities that advance the University’s academic mission and strengthen the Bryant University community. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: MA in Political Science or a closely related field. Experience teaching undergraduate political science courses. Commitment to active service in the department and University. Demonstrated understanding of AI relevancy to their discipline and its integration or applications in teaching. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Political Science or a closely related field. Ability to teach introductory and upper-level courses in U.S. and International Politics. An active research program is not required, but would be recognized and supported. Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC01648 Open Date 10/27/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Teaching Evaluation(s) Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4901": {
      "title": "Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Mathematics",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Mathematics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Mathematics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To receive full consideration, interested individuals must apply electronically through https://employment.bryant.edu/ . Applications should include a cover letter and curriculum vitae. The cover letter should describe the applicant’s teaching experience, courses they are qualified to teach, and approach to supporting students with diverse mathematical backgrounds. Applicants are encouraged to submit evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as teaching evaluations. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For questions about the position, please contact Dr. James Bishop, jabishop@bryant.edu, Search Committee Chair. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Mathematics Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Faculty Reports To Dean, College of Humanities and Social Sciences Position Summary Bryant University invites applications for a Non-Tenure Track Teaching Faculty position (Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor) in Mathematics in the Department of Mathematics and Economics. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, student success, and active participation in the department. We welcome applications from candidates with expertise in mathematics, applied mathematics, statistics, or related fields. We have a particular need for an individual who can teach undergraduate courses in introductory mathematics, statistics, and calculus. The ability to teach additional courses in applied mathematics, data analytics, or actuarial mathematics is desirable. Course descriptions are available through the Course Catalogue on the Bryant website. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030 , emphasizes a transformational learning experience through academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, and a connected community that supports belonging and success. Bryant is recognized as a top 1 percent national leader in student education outcomes and ROI and regularly receives high rankings from U.S. News and World Report, QS Stars, Money, Bloomberg Businessweek, Wall Street Journal, and College Factual. Bryant’s strategic plan, Vision 2030 , redefines higher education through a commitment to providing students with a transformational learning experience. Vision 2030 accelerates advancements in academic innovation, experiential learning, vibrant student life, Division I athletics, and a connected community that fosters belonging and success. Principal Accountabilities Teach undergraduate mathematics and statistics courses that support departmental programs and the University’s Impact Core curriculum. Develop engaging courses that emphasize quantitative reasoning, problem-solving, and practical applications. Provide academic support and mentoring to students with diverse backgrounds and levels of mathematical preparation. Collaborate with colleagues on course coordination, curriculum development, and assessment of student learning. Participate in departmental and University service, including admission events, student activities, and other initiatives that support student success. Demonstrate understanding of AI relevancy to their discipline and its integration or applications in teaching. Support domain specific AI tutoring resources within the Mathematics program. Qualifications Candidates must hold at least a master’s degree in mathematics, statistics, actuarial science, or a related quantitative field. A PhD is preferred. Successful candidates must demonstrate excellence in teaching, supported by strong teaching evaluations and a strong record of working with and supporting students. Candidates should be able to explain mathematical concepts clearly and engage students with varied levels of preparation. Experience incorporating technology and practical applications into teaching is desirable. Candidates should be willing to participate in departmental and University service, including admission events and student mentoring. Working Environment Bryant University is a private, student-centered institution accredited by the New England Commission of Higher Education ( NECHE ). Bryant is dedicated to educating and inspiring students to discover their passion, become innovative leaders with character, and make a difference around the world. Its academic programs emphasize practical applications, interdisciplinary collaboration, and experiential learning. The Department of Mathematics and Economics supports programs in Mathematics, Applied Mathematics and Statistics, Actuarial Mathematics, Business Economics, and the Master of Science in Actuarial Science. The department also provides foundational mathematics and statistics instruction to students across the University. Faculty collaborate on teaching, student research, curriculum development, and industry-connected learning opportunities. At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC01647 Open Date 10/27/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions To receive full consideration, interested individuals must apply electronically through https://employment.bryant.edu/ . Applications should include a cover letter and curriculum vitae. The cover letter should describe the applicant’s teaching experience, courses they are qualified to teach, and approach to supporting students with diverse mathematical backgrounds. Applicants are encouraged to submit evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as teaching evaluations. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For questions about the position, please contact Dr. James Bishop, jabishop@bryant.edu, Search Committee Chair. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Letter(s) of Recommendation Teaching Evaluation(s) Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.bryant.edu/postings/4899": {
      "title": "Grounds Worker",
      "description": "Bryant University Employment Opportunities | Grounds Worker Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academics at Bryant University Leadership Rankings and Accreditations Living in Rhode Island Contact Us Grounds Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Grounds Worker Full Time / Part Time Full Time Job Type Staff Reports To Manager of Grounds Position Summary Bryant University is a private New England university with a tradition of innovation and a global vision for success. Our new strategic plan, Vision 2030 , sets a trajectory for the next decade through academic excellence, outstanding student life, competitive athletics and student outcomes among the nation’s top 1% for ROI . The Grounds Worker reports to the Manager of Grounds and is accountable to perform all work related to the maintenance and repair of lawns, walks, roads, parking lots, gardens, and other grounds. This is a full-time position with excellent benefits. Principal Accountabilities Specific duties include but are not limited to: routine cleaning of grounds; shoveling snow; operating trucks and power equipment; leveling off ground; hauling and spreading topsoil; felling and removing trees, branches, etc.; digging ditches with pick and shovel; moving furniture and equipment; loading and unloading trucks and trailers; assisting trades people in their duties; performing minor painting, and other related duties as assigned. Certain requirements are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate persons with disabilities. Qualifications This position is best filled by an individual who has 4 or more years of commercial grounds and/or landscaping / snow removal experience, or equivalent education. They must be able to perform tasks requiring physical strength; possesses good hand-eye coordination; and be able to complete several tasks in specified time frames without immediate supervision. The ability to read, write and understand directions is required. A current valid Rhode Island Class 2 Operator’s driver’s license is required. RI Pesticide Licensure preferred. This position is subject to the successful completion of a pre-employment physical examination, criminal background check and division of motor vehicles check. This position requires the ability to exercise considerable physical effort in lifting and swinging an ax, pick, shovel, etc.; pushing lawn mowers and other grounds-related equipment; lifting, moving and swinging dead weight when necessary, and carrying supplies and materials. Position requires exposure to discomfort arising from having to work for long periods in the sun and heat, dampness, snow and cold. Certain requirements are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate persons with disabilities. Working Environment At Bryant University, we believe that our strength lies in the richness of our campus community and the unique perspectives that shape it. By connecting academic and social experiences, we create an environment where individuals feel valued, respected, and supported. Our commitment to fostering belonging and well-being ensures that everyone has the opportunity to thrive and contribute meaningfully. We encourage applications from those who appreciate the wide range of experiences and backgrounds that make our community exceptional. Discover more about how we cultivate a welcoming and collaborative campus culture that drives excellence. Physical Capacities Posting Detail Information Posting Number STA02824 Work Hours Monday – Friday – 7 am – 3:30 pm Open Date 08/31/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Special Instructions Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Letter(s) of Recommendation Office of Human Resources 1150 Douglas Pike Smithfield, RI 02918 Smithfield, RI Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Emergency Information © The Trustees of Bryant University bryant.edu Bryant Campus Map Campus Events To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
